  "result": "Put it in a shared/common location both modules depend on (e.g. `src/shared/formatCurrency.js` or `lib/shared/`), owned jointly or by a \"core\" team, rather than copying it into `reports/` and `billing/`. That avoids the cross-module dependency you're worried about (neither team imports from the other's folder) while keeping the logic in one place \u2014 copies tend to drift and cause bugs like inconsistent currency formatting across invoices and reports. The tradeoff is you need a lightweight convention for who can edit shared code (e.g. require review from both teams, or treat it as append-only/stable); if you genuinely expect billing and reports to need different formatting logic soon, forking now with clearly renamed functions (`formatCurrencyForInvoice` vs `formatCurrencyForReport`) is more honest than pretending it's still \"the same\" shared helper in two places.",
